# Assertions and Test Deduplication

## Meaningful Assertions

- Assert user-visible outcomes: URL, heading text, invoice number, cart count
- API: validate specific fields (`access_token`, `cart_items`, `invoice_number`)
- Avoid weak checks: `toBeTruthy()` on large objects without field checks
- One primary assertion per logical expectation; group related checks in same step

```javascript
// Weak
expect(body).toBeTruthy();

// Strong
expect(body.invoice_number).toMatch(/^INV-/);
expect(body.status).toBe('COMPLETED');
```

## Avoid Duplication

- Do not repeat login steps in every spec — use `authenticated` fixture
- Shared setup belongs in `beforeEach` or fixtures, not copy-pasted across files
- If UI and API cover the same AC, UI = E2E confidence, API = contract speed — do not duplicate identical assertions in both without reason
- Extract repeated API calls into helper methods (`createCartWithProduct()`)
